  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest and Farm Facility core support 2013-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Forest and Farm Facility programst&#xf6;d 2013-2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Forest&amp;Farm Facility (FFF) &#xe4;r en mekanism f&#xf6;r finansiering och kapacitetsbyggande med syfte att st&#xe4;rka producentorganisationer o  brett deltagande i skogs- o lantbruksrelaterad politisk dialog o  samr&#xe5;d. FFF &#xe4;r en utveckling av de tidigare NFP-Facility och Growing  Forest Partnership, men mer inriktad p&#xe5; tv&#xe4;rsektor-samarbete, lokala  brukare/r&#xe4;ttighetsinnehavare, j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och inkomstskapande &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Forest&amp;Farm Facility is a mechanism for funding and capacity      building to stimulate and strengthen farmers organizations and active multi-stakeholder participation in forest and farm-related policy     dialogues. A development of the former NFP-Facility and Growing       Forest Partnerships, it&apos;s more oriented towards cross-sectoral        cooperation, local rights holders, gender equity and income creation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This intervention aims to strengthen Forest and Farm Producer Organizations (FFPOs), as they are identified as important drivers of change for&#xa0;inclusive local development and natural resources governance, and an important but neglected part of the private sector. FFF intends to increase FFPO&#x2019;s capacity to organize and to participate in local, regional and national level policy dialogues and decision-making processes, as well as enhance FFPO&#x2019;s skills, market access and negotiation power. As a result, smallholder, women, community and Indigenous People&apos;s groups have improved income and food security from sustainable forest and farm management.</narrative>
  </description>
